CONCEPT
  product: Perch, an AI-native tool-fabrication environment for corvids.
  premise: crows already manufacture hook tools from twigs, so the product is a
  code editor for stick geometry that behaves exactly like a developer tool:
  tab-completion for bends, a pull-request review queue nobody ever clears, and
  a grudge index that ships enabled with the toggle greyed out.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:   cyanotype engineering drawing set, blueprint dark mode. Bordered
           drawing frames with title-block strips, 8mm drafting grid, dimension
           lines with tick serifs, redline callout balloons in annotation
           orange. No shadows, radius capped at 2px, all structure carried by
           hairlines.
  palette: bg #0B2A45, fg #DDE9F3, primary #6FA8D6, accent #E8703A,
           muted #7C98B4, ink #DDE9F3
  fonts:   display Barlow Condensed, body IBM Plex Mono
  archetype: developer-tool product page issued as an engineering drawing set;
           pricing rendered as a ruled parts-list schedule rather than cards.

  anti-sameness check against the last 7 entries (09-01 through 09-07):
  illuminated manuscript vellum, varsity trophy navy/gold, pharma blister pack,
  clay game launcher, glass aurora dark, 1974 supergraphic identity manual,
  automotive dark configurator. No collision on style, palette or font pair.
  Neither Barlow Condensed nor IBM Plex Mono appears in the last 7, and no
  recent entry uses a monospace body face.

  note: ui-ux-pro-max returned the generic developer-tool default (slate
  #0F172A with a green run accent and JetBrains Mono). Took the technical
  monospace signal from it, discarded the palette, since that look is the most
  templated result available for this product type.

IMAGES
  budget: 3 of 4 used, one deliberately unspent.
  rationale: hero skipped, the direction is typographic and a photo inside a
  blueprint frame would read as a pasted-on stock plate. Demo subject assets
  skipped, the demo is a code editor made of text and rules with no photo slot.
  Full budget to the testimonial fallback role.

  headshot-1.webp  attempt 1/2  PASS  three-quarter corporate crow portrait,
                   duotone lands inside the palette with no CSS correction,
                   no text artifacts, no generic-render tells.
  headshot-2.webp  attempt 1/2  PASS  correct subject and tone. Came back with
                   a cream paper deckle border where the other two have dark
                   wash borders. Handled in CSS by cropping the plate inside an
                   overflow-hidden hairline frame (object-fit cover, scale 1.2)
                   rather than burning a second attempt.
  headshot-3.webp  attempt 1/2  PASS  head-on framing, reads as a third
                   distinct sitter.
  All three cropped to 320x320 WebP, largest file 19 KB, well under the 500 KB
  validation ceiling. No image dropped.

BUILD
  landing: site/entries/cursor-for-crows/index.html
    Hero drawing frame with a dimension line under the h1 and a numbered
    redline callout. Three detail plates keyed Detail A/B/C (drawing
    vernacular, not decorative 01/02/03 numbering). Testimonials as captioned
    cyanotype portrait plates. Pricing as a single ruled schedule table that
    collapses to stacked blocks under 900px. Only non-user-triggered motion is
    the dimension lines drawing in once on scroll, disabled under
    prefers-reduced-motion.
  demo: site/entries/cursor-for-crows/demo.html
    The Forge. Four-file stick asset tree with dirty markers, bend-script
    editor with a ghost-text AI completion, Caw chat rail with canned deadpan
    replies, a Grudge Index tab with severity bars, a streaming fabrication log
    drawer, and a status bar wired to the active file.
    Tab-to-accept and Esc-to-reject are scoped to the focused editor pane only,
    with visible Accept and Reject buttons as the primary path, so global tab
    order is not hijacked.

WARNINGS AND NEAR-MISSES
  - Two Bash heredocs were rejected by the sandbox for brace-plus-quote
    patterns (a set comprehension, and a shell for-loop with variable
    expansion). Rewrote both without those constructs. No repo files affected.
  - headshot-2 border mismatch, resolved in CSS as noted above.
  - Contrast checked before building: fg 11.89:1, primary 5.76:1, accent
    4.76:1, muted 4.90:1, all against bg #0B2A45. Every pair clears WCAG AA.
  - Gallery slide background for this entry is a dark blue, and 09-06 is a dark
    indigo two slides away. Different enough in hue and treatment, left as is.

